{"Title":"An Act to increase the penalty for school tardiness","BillNumber":"H1415","DocketNumber":"HD1637","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"T_C1","Name":"Tackey Chan","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/T_C1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-12T17:05:24.85"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"T_C1","Name":"Tackey Chan","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/T_C1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-12T17:05:24.85"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H1415/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Chan of Quincy, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 1415) of Tackey Chan for legislation to increase the penalty assessed on parents or guardians for excessive school truancy of a child.  The Judiciary.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 2 of Chapter 76 of the General Laws is hereby amended in line 5 by striking out the words “be punished by a fine of not more than twenty dollars” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- “be punished by a fine of not more than fifty dollars for each day that the child does not attend school.”\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J19","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J19"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}